+// Without a context snapshot, the main thread's main world is built as if it
+// came from one: the interface templates of the types a snapshot holds are
+// made with no runtime-enabled feature on, as a snapshot's are, and each
+// context gets the runtime-enabled properties of those types afterwards.
+// The global object then lists its properties in the order a browser with a
+// snapshot gives (the runtime-enabled ones after the others).
+bool g_emulating_snapshot = false;
+
+bool EmulatesContextSnapshot(const DOMWrapperWorld& world) {
+  return g_emulating_snapshot && IsMainThread() && world.IsMainWorld();
+}
